# Pinned `spec` revision the conformance runner validates against.
#
# The runner refuses to run if the spec checkout it is given is not at this
# commit (override with --allow-spec-drift when deliberately testing against
# unreleased vocabulary). Without a pin the suite silently tracks whatever is
# on spec `main`, so a run that passed yesterday can pass today for a
# different reason.
#
# To re-pin: check out the new spec revision, put its full SHA and its
# VOCAB_VERSIONS line below, run `make -C . conformance` (or
# `scripts/run_conformance.py`), and record the resulting counts in the PR.

# PINNED at 2162718, the MERGE commit of the-cascade-protocol/spec PR #72 on
# `main` (clinical v1.20: the clinical:narrativeText comment restated as the
# canonical spelling for FHIR text.div and C-CDA section text alike, and the
# new clinical:documentType, a human-readable document-type label distinct
# from the closed-slug cascade:documentType; core v3.10, health v2.11,
# coverage v1.6 unchanged). Tag `vocab/clinical-v1.20` points at this commit.
# It replaces the pin below, 735bb57.
#
# WHAT MOVING THE PIN DID. Three new shapes in clinical.shapes.ttl, all
# sh:Warning per the core v3.5 ratchet: clinical:NarrativeTextCountShape
# (sh:maxCount 1 on clinical:narrativeText, relaxed from the sh:Violation it
# carried on ClinicalDocumentShape through v1.19), clinical:DocumentTypeShape
# (sh:datatype xsd:string, sh:maxCount 1 on the new clinical:documentType) and
# clinical:NarrativeTextSpellingShape (sh:targetSubjectsOf cascade:narrativeText
# and sh:targetSubjectsOf clinical:content, sh:maxCount 0 on each -- the
# migration-window signal for the two undeclared spellings a C-CDA import path
# wrote before this release). All three target the same seven document
# classes the v1.16 status shapes do.
#
# Four fixtures added in fixtures/clinical/: document-ccda-section-narrative
# .VALID (the release's target state -- one clinical:narrativeText, one
# clinical:documentType, no legacy spelling), document-legacy-narrative
# -spelling.WARN (the same text on both cascade:narrativeText and
# clinical:content, no clinical:narrativeText -- the pre-release importer's
# actual output; two sh:Warning results, zero sh:Violation),
# document-documenttype-repeated.WARN (two clinical:documentType values; one
# sh:Warning from DocumentTypeShape's own sh:maxCount 1, zero sh:Violation)
# and document-narrative-text-repeated.WARN (two clinical:narrativeText
# values, modelling the exact scenario NarrativeTextCountShape's own comment
# names -- two C-CDA sections sharing one LOINC section code converting onto
# one section record; one sh:Warning from NarrativeTextCountShape's own
# sh:maxCount 1, zero sh:Violation). See fixtures/clinical/INVENTORY.md.
#
# Measured on this branch's fixture set (194 fixtures) against both revisions:
#   735bb57 (old pin): 163 passed / 27 failed / 0 skipped / 190 total, 64,847
#     constraint checks.
#   2162718 (new pin): 167 passed / 27 failed / 0 skipped / 194 total, 65,053
#     constraint checks.
#
# ZERO pre-existing verdicts change. Compared entry by entry across both runs
# (outcome, reason and constraint-check count), 0 of the 190 pre-existing
# fixtures differ in outcome or reason. Five of them (the document and
# document-subtype fixtures the two new class-targeted shapes also reach) pick
# up one or two additional constraint checks each -- 8 total -- and none trips
# a warning. The 27 that fail at 2162718 are byte-identical, as (fixture,
# reason) pairs, to the 27 already enumerated in KNOWN_FAILURES.json, whose
# specPin is advanced to 2162718 in this same commit, so the ratchet holds.
#
# RED-first, against 735bb57 with --allow-spec-drift, selecting only the four
# new files: 1 passed / 3 failed / 4 total, 188 constraint checks. The two
# spelling/documentType WARN fixtures report NO_WARNING there; the VALID
# fixture already passes, at 44 checks, which is what an additive release
# means for a record with no legacy spelling. document-narrative-text-repeated
# .WARN is RED there in the sharper way this constraint's relaxation is
# actually about: it is REJECTED, not merely unnoticed -- reported VIOLATIONS,
# clinical:ClinicalDocumentShape's own sh:maxCount 1 on clinical:narrativeText
# firing at its default severity, because through v1.19 this constraint lived
