#
# 6b34e94 is in fact still reachable from `main`, as the merge preserved it, so
# unlike the draft pin before it this one was never unresolvable. That is not
# why it moves. A branch head is not a release identity: it names one side of a
# merge rather than the state `main` actually publishes, nothing guarantees it
# survives a rebase or a branch deletion, and it is not what the version tag
# points at. The pin names the commit the release is published as.
#
# Tag `vocab/clinical-v1.19` points at this commit (pushed 2026-09-07). Tags
